1. NON-COMMERCIALIZATION

The Software, in whole or in part, and any fork, derivative work, or modified
version thereof, may not be sold, licensed for a fee, offered as part of a paid
product or service, placed behind a paywall or subscription, or otherwise
commercialized without explicit written permission from the applicable
copyright holders.

Commercialization includes, but is not limited to:

* Selling the Software or any fork or modified version of it
* Requiring payment to download, access, or use the Software
* Placing the Software, a fork, or any of its features behind a paywall,
  subscription, membership, or other paid access system
* Selling access to modified or exclusive builds of the Software
* Using the Software or a substantial portion of it as part of a commercial
  product or paid service

Voluntary donations, tips, sponsorships, and crowdfunding are permitted.

Receiving donations or other voluntary financial support does not by itself
constitute commercialization under this License, regardless of whether the
recipient develops, maintains, modifies, or distributes the Software or a fork
of it.

Donations must remain voluntary and may not be required in exchange for access
to the Software, a fork, features, patches, builds, downloads, or functionality.

2. ATTRIBUTION FOR FORKS AND DERIVATIVE WORKS

Forks, derivative works, and modified versions must clearly identify VRCNext
as the original project and must not misrepresent the origin or authorship of
the original work.

Existing copyright, license, and attribution notices included with the Software
must not be intentionally removed or misrepresented.

Maintainers of forks are encouraged, but not required, to include a contributor
list in their repository, such as in the README, CREDITS file, or equivalent.

When practical, this list should preserve the names or usernames of VRCNext
contributors who had contributed to the project at the time the fork was
created, as well as appropriate attribution for contributors to prior forks
from which the fork is directly derived.

Maintainers are not required to continuously synchronize their contributor
list with contributors who join the original VRCNext project after the fork
was created.

Failure to maintain such a contributor list does not constitute a violation of
this License, provided that the required attribution and existing notices
described above are preserved.

